    </codeType>
    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThere \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Ebe no blind spots (hiding places or secluded areas) created on all streets through the placement of any structures, including trees and vegetation. This may include ensuring that: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Etrees have 1.8 metres clear stems to maintain visibility at ground level \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ethe height of any planting at maturity is taken into account \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ebuilding layouts prioritise passive surveillance by ensuring clear sightlines to public and shared spaces \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eabove-ground utilities structures, such as substations, meter boxes, or bin stores, are carefully located and designed to avoid creating hidden areas \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eboundary treatments do not obstruct sightlines or create concealed spaces\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
